# Cloudflare Pages response headers (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/).
# Ignored by other hosts; docker/web/nginx.conf is the self-hosted equivalent.
#
# Permissions-Policy allows `camera` for the invite QR scanner. There is no CSP: Flutter loads
# CanvasKit/fonts from gstatic and needs wasm-unsafe-eval, so a CSP must be tested against the
# real build before enabling.
#
# One rule on purpose: Pages joins repeated headers from overlapping rules with a comma instead of
# replacing them, so a second rule for static assets would corrupt Cache-Control.
#
# Caching: Flutter web files are not content-hashed (main.dart.js, flutter_bootstrap.js, assets/*,
# version.json, firebase-*.js keep their names across releases). `no-cache` makes the browser
# revalidate with the ETag Pages sends (a cheap 304 when nothing changed), so a new release is
# picked up on the next load. Flutter 3.41's flutter_service_worker.js is only a stub that
# unregisters older caching workers (the app has no offline asset cache), and web/firebase-messaging-sw.js must also stay revalidated: the browser
# checks service worker scripts for updates, and a stale copy would pin an old push handler.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
